# THE SPATIAL LATENT UPSCALER PIN — empty means "do not bake one".
#
# One line, "<huggingface-repo> <revision-sha>", to turn multi-scale generation
# on. Blank or absent and the media image is built exactly as it is today:
# ltxcaps reports latent_upsampler_baked=false, videogen records
# upscaler_absent_reason=latent-upsampler-not-baked on every clip, and the
# single-scale path runs unchanged.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS AT ALL, rather than a default the build could apply
# on its own. A revision is the licence. The LTX transformer above it is
# pinned to 8984fa25007f376c1a299016d0957a37a2f797bb because the owner
# accepted the LTX Open Weights terms as they stood at those exact bytes; the
# spatial upscaler ships under the same family of terms and gets the same
# treatment. An agent cannot accept a licence on the owner's behalf, and
# writing a plausible-looking sha here would be a fabrication wearing the
# costume of a fact.
#
# WHAT ENABLING IT BUYS, and it is the largest single quality lever left.
# Measured arithmetic: the generation canvas is 704 wide and the delivered
# film is 1080 wide, so assembly resamples every frame UP by 1.534x. A pixel
# resampler cannot invent detail that was never sampled — that 53% is the
# softness a viewer reads as "hazy", and it is baked in before Remotion ever
# opens the clip. With the upscaler present videogen generates at 704x1248,
# upsamples the LATENTS 2x, runs a short partial re-denoise at 1408x2496 so
# the transformer actually synthesises the new detail, and only then decodes.
# The film's 1080 then becomes a DOWNSCALE of real detail.
#
# COST, computed from the architecture in diffusers 0.38.0
# (pipelines/ltx/modeling_latent_upsampler.py): 126.25 M parameters,
# ~482 MiB fp32 / ~241 MiB bf16 — roughly 1.2% of the ~40 GiB media image.
# Disk is not the blocker here. GPU time is unmeasured: the refine pass adds
# ltxcaps.REFINE_STEPS steps at 4x the pixels, which is real additional
# inference and must be measured on a real generation before any cost claim
# is made about it.
#
# TO ENABLE: uncomment and complete the line below with the repository and
# the exact revision whose licence terms have been read and accepted. The
# build then verifies, and refuses if any of it does not hold — the revision
# must resolve to that sha, a LICENSE or NOTICE must ship with the weights,
# config.json must declare LTXLatentUpsamplerModel, the config must load
# under the installed diffusers, and the weights must be inside the size
# guard.
#
# <huggingface-repo> <revision-sha>
